From 45fd6dc770ef815403cb23f1f1e44644b2085b74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PingoLee <eurafael@msn.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:50:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] scheduler: add an experimental fair class for spawned
 tasks

`Threads.@spawn fair=true` marks a root task. Until it first runs, a marked
root waits in FIFO rings, stamped at insert, instead of the priority heaps;
a pop samples two rings and takes the older head. Once it has started, it
and every task it first makes runnable are queued in a second set of the
stock heaps. When both that work and other tasks are waiting, a thread
shares its time between the two by a weight (`JULIA_SCHED_FAIR_WEIGHT`,
default 1/2), so closed-loop clients that spawn work and wait on it are
served in about the order they arrived instead of being starved by newer
work. Only `:default` tasks are classed. The class is one byte, the last
padding byte of the first cache line of `jl_task_t`. Until something is
marked, the scheduler's entry points take the stock path after one load
of a flag.

The keyword and the variable are experimental and may change.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)
